<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">First Dominican Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1844 CE – 1861 CE · capital Santo Domingo</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The first Dominican republic, won from Haiti in 1844 and dominated by the rival strongmen Pedro Santana and Buenaventura Báez until its annexation by Spain.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/secret-society">secret society</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/la-trinitaria">La Trinitaria</a>, founded in 1838 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-pablo-duarte">Juan Pablo Duarte</a>, organised resistance to Haitian rule. On 27 February 1844 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-del-rosario-sanchez">Francisco del Rosario Sánchez</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramon-matias-mella">Ramón Matías Mella</a> proclaimed independence at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puerta-del-conde">Puerta del Conde</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santo-domingo">Santo Domingo</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> rancher <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-santana">Pedro Santana</a> defeated the Haitian army and soon exiled Duarte and the other founders.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The constitution of San Cristóbal of November 1844 included Article 210, giving <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-santana">Santana</a> dictatorial powers. Santana and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buenaventura-baez">Buenaventura Báez</a> alternated in power, each seeking foreign protection from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> or the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a>. The country repeatedly defended itself against Haitian invasions under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/faustin-soulouque">Faustin Soulouque</a>, notably at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-las-carreras">Las Carreras</a> in 1849 and at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-santome">Santomé</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sabana-larga">Sabana Larga</a> in 1855 to 1856. Tobacco from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cibao">Cibao</a> valley and mahogany were the main exports; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/printing-press">printing</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paper-money">paper money</a> caused ruinous <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inflation">inflation</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Fearing renewed Haitian attack and seeking to keep power, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-santana">Santana</a> negotiated the country's annexation to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, proclaimed on 18 March 1861, creating the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/province-of-santo-domingo-1861-1865">Province of Santo Domingo</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/first-dominican-republic.jpg" alt="First Dominican Republic" width="320" height="201"><figcaption>Image: BetacommandBot · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Dominican_Republic_(1844).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1844 CE – 1861 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Santo Domingo</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Pedro Santana, Buenaventura Báez</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Spanish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/dominican-republic">Dominican Republic</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Dominican Republic (1844-1861)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1852&amp;focus=first-dominican-republic" aria-label="First Dominican Republic on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2785 1493 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where First Dominican Republic lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M3105 1749L3041 1746M3105 1749L3105 1749"/><path class="map-dot-n" 